    "body": "> Report is already exposed in gecko\r\n\r\nWhen was that added? [MDN BCD doesn't have it](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Report) and I definitely don't see it in Firefox 107. Maybe Firefox will hit the web compat issues before Chrome?\r\n\r\n> Because that's the platform convention and matches idiomatic JS.\r\n\r\nOk. Should there perhaps be a non-normative note saying that while in the past it was common to use [NoInterfaceObject], this is discouraged in order to match idiomatic JS?",
